1. Why Testing Matters?
-->Testing is important because it ensures that the application works correctly and helps identify bugs before deployment.
-->In enterprise systems, testing improves reliability, data accuracy, and user trust.
Benefits of Testing:
  ->Prevents bugs and errors
  ->Improves system reliability
  ->Ensures business requirements are met
  ->Reduces maintenance costs
  ->Increases user confidence
2. What is Asynchronous Apex?
-->Asynchronous Apex allows code to run in the background instead of making users wait for long operations to finish. 
-->It is useful for handling large amounts of data and time-consuming processes.
Examples:
  ->Sending bulk emails
  ->Generating large reports
  ->Synchronizing data with external systems
Types:
  ->Future Methods
  ->Queueable Apex
  ->Batch Apex
  ->Scheduled Apex
3. What is Salesforce DX?
-->Salesforce DX (Developer Experience) is a modern development framework that helps developers build, test, and deploy Salesforce applications efficiently.
Features:
  ->Source-driven development
  ->Better team collaboration
  ->Integration with GitHub
  ->Easy deployment and testing
  ->Supports CI/CD practices
4. Complete System Workflow (College Management System)?
  ->Student Registration Process
  ->Student submits registration form.
  ->Validation Rules verify required fields and data accuracy.
  ->Record is saved in Salesforce database.
  ->Flow sends a confirmation email to the student.
  ->Apex Trigger updates course enrollment count.
  ->Formula fields automatically recalculate available seats.
  ->Platform Event sends notifications to faculty if needed.
  ->Reports and dashboards update automatically.
  ->Administrators can monitor all activities and analytics.
  ->This workflow ensures that all processes happen automatically and accurately.
5. Important Test Cases?
1. Invalid Email Address
 ->Test: Enter an incorrect email format.
 ->Risk if not tested: Notifications may fail.
2. Duplicate Student Registration
  ->Test: Register the same student twice.
  ->Risk if not tested: Duplicate records may be created.
3. Course Overbooking
  ->Test: Enroll students after course capacity is reached.
  ->Risk if not tested: More students than available seats.
4. Attendance Calculation
  ->Test: Verify attendance percentage calculations.
  ->Risk if not tested: Incorrect warnings and reports.
5. Trigger Execution
  ->Test: Ensure triggers run after record creation.
  ->Risk if not tested: Automated actions may fail.
6. Async Thinking – Background Processing Examples?
1. Sending Bulk Emails
-->Large numbers of emails should be sent in the background to avoid slowing down the system.
2. Report Generation
-->Complex reports may take time and should run asynchronously.
3. Data Synchronization
-->Data exchange with external systems should happen in the background for better performance.
7. Reflection:Why Enterprise Software Development Needs Structured Workflows
  ->Enterprise software projects involve many developers and complex requirements. 
  ->Structured workflows help maintain code quality, improve collaboration, track changes, and reduce deployment risks. 
  ->Tools like GitHub, Salesforce DX, and CLI make development more organized and efficient.

Revision Questions and Answers
1. Why are tests important in enterprise systems?
  ->Tests ensure the system works correctly and prevent bugs from reaching users.
2. What problems happen without testing?
 ->Systems may contain bugs, incorrect calculations, security issues, and unreliable functionality.
3. Why is asynchronous processing useful?
 ->It allows long-running tasks to execute in the background without affecting user experience.
4. Difference between synchronous and asynchronous processing?
 ->Synchronous: Tasks execute one after another, and users wait for completion.
 ->Asynchronous: Tasks run in the background while users continue working.
5. Why do developers use version control?
 ->Version control tracks changes, supports collaboration, and allows rollback when needed.
6. Why is GitHub important?
 ->GitHub stores code, tracks versions, manages collaboration, and supports project development.
7. Why is DX useful for teams?
 ->Salesforce DX provides a standardized workflow, better collaboration, and easier deployments.
8. How do Flows, Triggers, and Validation Rules work together?
 ->Validation Rules check data, Flows automate processes, and Triggers handle advanced business logic.
9. Why should business logic be tested carefully?
 ->Incorrect business logic can cause wrong calculations, automation failures, and data inconsistencies.
10. Why is developer workflow important in large teams?
 ->It ensures consistency, improves collaboration, reduces conflicts, and increases productivity.
